//? Title: SmoothGrad:explicit noisy observations and signed gradient means
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Local image-score gradients can vary sharply across nearby inputs. Average ordinary fixed-target raw-score derivatives over a saved Gaussian bank for genuine MNIST images,and inspect finite-sample uncertainty,off-domain inputs,and clipping,target and initialization controls.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/smoothgrad.cpp`.

> The method

With fixed classc,standardized noisesz_kand scalesigma,the primary estimator is the signed mean:

$$ \widehat g=\frac1K\sum_{k=1}^K\nabla_x s_c(x+\sigma z_k),\qquad SE_i=\sqrt{\widehat{Var}(g_i)/K}. $$
\alttext(Average ordinary raw-score gradients over the explicit noisy inputs;coordinate standard errors use the unbiased sample variance divided by sample count.)

All points,ordinary derivatives,statistics and plot values remain tensors. The Gaussian bank is explicit,paired controls share it,and clipped inputs define a separate estimator. No new model fit or optimizer is needed for this frozen-model MonteCarlo average.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/smoothgrad_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/smoothgrad_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/smoothgrad_concept.tikz > build/smoothgrad_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/smoothgrad_concept.svg build/smoothgrad_concept.dvi > build/smoothgrad_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
